Current-binding removal
=======================

rtest_mset.mac loads unbinding-check.lisp. The appended checks cover
MAXIMA-MAKUNBOUND and the interpreter, debugger, parallel runner, REMVALUE
and label-removal paths which use it. Run them with the ordinary suite:

  timeout 120 ./maxima-local --no-init \
    --batch-string='run_testsuite(tests=["rtest_mset"]);'

On ECL 21.2.1, CL:MAKUNBOUND removes the global symbol value while leaving
an active PROGV binding unchanged. ECL's tagged src/c/assignment.d uses
ECL_SET for CL_MAKUNBOUND and ECL_SETQ for CL_SET. The Maxima compatibility
helper uses the latter accessor for a nonconstant symbol's current value.
Invalid arguments and constants retain CL:MAKUNBOUND's checks and errors.
The helper checks the actual constant flag; CONSTANTP may expand a symbol
macro and does not identify a constant variable reliably. Symbol-macro
regressions also require that removal does not invoke the macroexpander.
On other Lisps the helper delegates to CL:MAKUNBOUND. The Common Lisp
function itself is unchanged. References:

https://gitlab.com/embeddable-common-lisp/ecl/-/blob/21.2.1/src/c/assignment.d
https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/f_makunb.htm
https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/s_progv.htm

The tests use fresh uninterned symbols with separately checked global,
outer and inner values. They cover bound/unbound scopes, normal return,
errors and THROW; MBINDING cleanup; debugger removal and restoration;
captured unbound values and multiple return values; REMVALUE's known,
reset and unknown variables; label removal; invalid inputs/constants;
and 64 generated global-value cases. Every outer value is checked again
after unwinding, so a locally plausible result cannot hide global damage.

Execution sites include serial calls, forced calling runners and workers,
the serial fallback and the public scheduler. On native SBCL, CCL and ECL,
two synchronized threads also remove the value of the same symbol from
their respective PROGV bindings while checking both local and global
state. Waits are bounded; started threads are joined during cleanup.
Threadless Lisps retain the portable checks.

This change corrects value removal. It does not yet give ordinary Maxima
function parameters or BLOCK locals their own dynamic bindings. Those
shared value cells require a separate change to the scopes owning MBIND.
It also does not make shared symbol properties private.
